  "worked_solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $v(x)={5}^{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot {5}^{x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot ({5}^{x})^{′}}{{({5}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot {5}^{x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot {5}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{{({5}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5)}{{({5}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{{5}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
